While most CFMGs have held elections, have term limits for executive officers and employ honorary forest officers (HFOs), other governance processes were not as consistently implemented. Most CFMGs have not opened bank accounts, do not maintain a receipt book, or issue forest-use permits. Financial and annual reporting to community members was also apparently rarely implemented.

It appears that most CFMGs have not held elections since they were formed, up to five years ago (@fig-last_election).


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Number of years since the last CFMG executive election. The length of each bar segment represents the proportion of CFMGs in that category. The numbers superimposed on the bars represent the actual number of CFMGs in each category.](CFMG-Governance_files/figure-html/fig-last_election-1.png){#fig-last_election width=672}
:::
:::


::: return-to-summary
[← Return to Summary](Summary.html#governance)
:::

Forty-three out of 75 CFMGs have not held elections for over 3 yrs, although term limits for executive officers are typically 2-3 years (@fig-tenure). This indicates that most CFMGs are not in compliance with their By-laws & Constitutions.


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Tenure of CFMG executive positions. The length of each bar segment represents the proportion of CFMGs with that tenure length. The numbers superimposed on the bars represent the actual number of CFMGs in each category.](CFMG-Governance_files/figure-html/fig-tenure-1.png){#fig-tenure width=672}
:::
:::


In contrast, most CFMGs do appear to be holding meetings regularly (@fig-meetings). However, a small proportion of CFMGs holds meetings only rarely or never.


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Number of CFMG meetings per year. The length of each bar segment represents the proportion of CFMGs with the specified meeting frequency. The numbers superimposed on the bars represent the actual number of CFMGs in each category.](CFMG-Governance_files/figure-html/fig-meetings-1.png){#fig-meetings width=672}
:::
:::


## CFMG business processes

As with the legal processes, we asked CFMG executives about the state of their business processes. Specifically, we asked if they had developed annual workplans and budgets, and whether these plans were being implemented. We also asked if they had developed a business plan and if any forest user groups had been established (@tbl-business_processes).


